          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Why is osteoarthritis not simply “wear and tear” of a joint?",
          "answer": "Osteoarthritis is not simply \"wear and tear\" of a joint because it is a complex disorder impacting the entire joint structure, including cartilage, bone, ligaments, and muscles. The characterization of osteoarthritis as merely \"wear and tear\" is misleading; it can imply that the condition is due solely to mechanical erosion, which overlooks the active processes involved. Osteoarthritis involves inflammation and attempts at repair, rather than just degeneration.\n\nMoreover, resting the joint in response to pain can lead to muscle weakness, worsening the condition rather than protecting the joint. Current guidelines recommend exercise as a primary treatment to strengthen muscles and enhance joint function, contrary to the old belief that a worn joint should be rested (source: General clinical reference on osteoarthritis).\n\nI cannot provide in-depth details about specific treatment protocols or further specifics on the underlying biological mechanisms beyond what was summarized.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
